## 3. L1 — Instrumenting Dagster's own processes

All three long-lived components are ordinary Python processes, so standard OTel Python auto-instrumentation applies.

### 3.1 Manual wrapper

```bash
pip install \
  opentelemetry-distro \
  opentelemetry-exporter-otlp \
  opentelemetry-instrumentation-grpc \
  opentelemetry-instrumentation-asgi \
  opentelemetry-instrumentation-requests

opentelemetry-bootstrap -a install   # auto-detects installed libs
```

| Component | Original command | With OTel |
|---|---|---|
| webserver | `dagster-webserver -h 0.0.0.0 -p 80` | `opentelemetry-instrument dagster-webserver -h 0.0.0.0 -p 80` |
| daemon | `dagster-daemon run` | `opentelemetry-instrument dagster-daemon run` |
| code server | `dagster api grpc -h 0.0.0.0 -p 3030 -m my_module` | `opentelemetry-instrument dagster api grpc ...` |

What this buys you:

- **webserver** — GraphQL/HTTP spans via ASGI instrumentation. Answers "why is Dagit slow", "which query is hammering Postgres".
- **code server** — gRPC server spans. Shows daemon ↔ code-location latency and definitions-load time.
- **daemon** — sensor/schedule ticks appear as gRPC *client* spans against code servers.

> ⚠️ **Disable SQLAlchemy/psycopg2 instrumentation.** Dagster writes hundreds to thousands of event-log rows per run. Full DB span coverage will flood your trace backend, cost real money, and measurably slow runs down. Set `OTEL_PYTHON_DISABLED_INSTRUMENTATIONS=sqlalchemy,psycopg2` and only enable it temporarily when debugging DB issues.

### 3.2 OTel Operator auto-injection (no Dockerfile CMD changes)

```yaml
apiVersion: opentelemetry.io/v1alpha1
kind: Instrumentation
metadata:
  name: dagster-python
  namespace: dagster
spec:
  exporter:
    endpoint: http://otel-agent.observability:4318
  propagators: [tracecontext, baggage]
  sampler:
    type: parentbased_traceidratio
    argument: "0.1"
  python:
    env:
      - name: OTEL_PYTHON_DISABLED_INSTRUMENTATIONS
        value: "sqlalchemy,psycopg2"
```

Then annotate pods with `instrumentation.opentelemetry.io/inject-python: "dagster/dagster-python"`.

⚠️ Injection works via a **mutating admission webhook on pod creation**. Dagster's **run pods are created at runtime by the K8sRunLauncher**, not by your Helm chart — so the annotation must go in `runLauncher.config.k8sRunLauncher.runK8sConfig.podTemplateSpecMetadata.annotations`. See §6.

