## 6. Helm values for the EKS deployment

The official chart has **four** places that need environment variables. Missing any one produces a blind spot.

```yaml
# usw2sandbox-values.yaml

# ---------- 1. Webserver ----------
dagsterWebserver:
  env:
    - name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME
      value: dagster-webserver
    - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
      value: http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317
    - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL
      value: grpc
    - name: OTEL_PYTHON_DISABLED_INSTRUMENTATIONS
      value: sqlalchemy,psycopg2
    - name: OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER
      value: parentbased_traceidratio
    - name: OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG
      value: "0.1"
    - name: OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES
      value: deployment.environment=sandbox,service.namespace=data-platform

# ---------- 2. Daemon (sensors and run_status_sensors execute here) ----------
dagsterDaemon:
  env:
    - name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME
      value: dagster-daemon
    - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
      value: http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317
    - name: OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER
      value: always_on            # trace root — never sample this away
    - name: OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES
      value: deployment.environment=sandbox

# ---------- 3. Code locations (gRPC servers) ----------
dagster-user-deployments:
  enabled: true
  deployments:
    - name: analytics
      image:
        repository: <registry>/analytics
        tag: "..."
      dagsterApiGrpcArgs: ["--module-name", "analytics.definitions"]
      port: 3030
      env:
        - name: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME
          value: dagster-code-analytics
        - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
          value: http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317

# ---------- 4. Run pods (most commonly missed) ----------
runLauncher:
  type: K8sRunLauncher
  config:
    k8sRunLauncher:
      envVars:                     # NOTE: plain KEY=VALUE strings only
        - "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-agent.observability.svc.cluster.local:4317"
        - "OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc"
        - "OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=dagster-run"
        - "OTEL_BSP_SCHEDULE_DELAY=1000"
        - "OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL=5000"
        - "OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio"
      envConfigMaps:
        - name: otel-config        # cleaner when you have many code locations
      runK8sConfig:
        podTemplateSpecMetadata:
          annotations:
            instrumentation.opentelemetry.io/inject-python: "dagster/dagster-python"
        podSpecConfig:
          terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30   # room for the final span flush
```

Pointing at the node-local agent instead of the Service avoids a cross-node hop, but `envVars` only accepts literal strings — no `valueFrom`. Use `runK8sConfig.containerConfig.env` for that:

```yaml
runK8sConfig:
  containerConfig:
    env:
      - name: NODE_IP
        valueFrom:
          fieldRef: { fieldPath: status.hostIP }
      - name: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
        value: "http://$(NODE_IP):4317"
```

