## 7. L3 — Run-level metrics from the event log

Some things are only knowable after the fact: queue time, retry counts, materialization freshness. `run_status_sensor` is the hook.

```python
from dagster import (
    run_status_sensor, RunStatusSensorContext,
    DagsterRunStatus, DefaultSensorStatus,
)
from opentelemetry import metrics
from .otel import init_otel

init_otel()
_meter = metrics.get_meter("dagster.runs")

_runs      = _meter.create_counter("dagster.run.completed")
_run_dur   = _meter.create_histogram("dagster.run.duration", unit="s")
_queue_dur = _meter.create_histogram("dagster.run.queue_duration", unit="s")


def _emit(context: RunStatusSensorContext, status: str):
    run = context.dagster_run
    stats = context.instance.get_run_stats(run.run_id)
    labels = {
        "job_name": run.job_name,
        "status": status,
        "code_location": (
            run.external_job_origin.location_name
            if run.external_job_origin else "unknown"
        ),
    }
    _runs.add(1, labels)
    if stats.start_time and stats.end_time:
        _run_dur.record(stats.end_time - stats.start_time, labels)
    if stats.enqueued_time and stats.launch_time:
        _queue_dur.record(stats.launch_time - stats.enqueued_time, labels)


@run_status_sensor(run_status=DagsterRunStatus.SUCCESS,
                   default_status=DefaultSensorStatus.RUNNING)
def on_success(context): _emit(context, "success")


@run_status_sensor(run_status=DagsterRunStatus.FAILURE,
                   default_status=DefaultSensorStatus.RUNNING)
def on_failure(context): _emit(context, "failure")


@run_status_sensor(run_status=DagsterRunStatus.CANCELED,
                   default_status=DefaultSensorStatus.RUNNING)
def on_cancel(context): _emit(context, "canceled")
```

> These sensors run **in the daemon process**, so the daemon image needs the OTel dependencies and a working `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`.
>
> Sensors are tick-driven (30s default). Metrics lag, and events can be missed across daemon restarts. If you need strict accuracy for alerting, prefer the kube-state-metrics path from §2.3 and use these for analytics.

### Recommended metric set

| Metric | Type | Labels (**never `run_id`**) |
|---|---|---|
| `dagster.run.completed` | Counter | job_name, status, code_location |
| `dagster.run.duration` | Histogram | job_name, code_location |
| `dagster.run.queue_duration` | Histogram | job_name |
| `dagster.run.in_progress` | UpDownCounter | code_location |
| `dagster.op.duration` | Histogram | job_name, op_name |
| `dagster.asset.materialization` | Counter | asset_key, status |
| `dagster.asset.rows_written` | Histogram | asset_key |
| `dagster.sensor.tick` | Counter | sensor_name, status |
| `dagster.step.retries` | Counter | job_name, op_name |

